    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate prioritizing stolen base upside and favorable platoon alignments, anchored by **Corbin Carroll** (73.48) and **Tyler Soderstrom** (76.91). **Tyler Soderstrom** represents the highest-scoring play of the day, buoyed by an aggressive +10% park factor and an advantageous #2 spot in the order against a beatable arm in Peralta. Meanwhile, **Corbin Carroll** remains a perennial engine for the squad; his matchup against Hughes is ideal, and his sprint speed profile provides the elite floor our 5x5 Roto strategy demands. **Isaac Paredes** (63.56) is also a strong start assuming he slots into the #3 hole, as the dynamic platoon advantage against Tidwell\u2014coupled with favorable wind conditions\u2014outweighs his neutral park projection.\n\nWhile we are deep on talent, the bench remains a source of frustration due to the current IL congestion. **James Wood** and **Vinnie Pasquantino** remain sidelined, while **Josh Naylor** and **Jose Caballero** are inactive due to scheduled team off-days. Consequently, the rotation is currently devoid of high-end bench threats to push our active starters. **Austin Riley** (50.50) is the most volatile asset in today's lineup; he narrowly avoided a benching due to a lack of viable alternatives and a lingering 37% rain risk that threatens a short outing. **Mickey Moniak** (61.43) is the surprise performer in our OF rankings today, capitalizing on a significant +14% platoon boost against Soroka. We are effectively betting on **Mickey Moniak** to maintain his efficiency while praying that **Austin Riley** avoids a weather-shortened disaster in a bottom-of-the-order role.",
